Z||000003||MooCow||03-25-2001||10:58 PM||||Wow  So how much are these Rims??  And do you actually think they would fit well?? <BR>I love the look of smooth seems.  So has anyone actually done it before??<P>                             Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kensig_1.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny.  Soon will be Viper Yellow!||||reg||4
Z||000004||Tina||03-25-2001||11:07 PM||||I see your up to no good again  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Just wanted to thanks again.<BR>Helped me out a lot.<BR>The body shop has the pic now, you made for me. Even they were impressed.<P>In about three weeks it becomes reality.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||TwisT||03-25-2001||11:21 PM||||Ken,<P>I haven't seriously shopped around yet for best pricing.  One place I found asks $320 a peice (!) but keep in mind that's just for the rim by itself.  They usually give you a much better price when you buy the wheel/tire package as a whole.  I should be able to get a set of four with tires for around $1500.  Not cheap,  but to me,  worth every penny for the end result.  This rim should fit nicely,  actually,  because it is a FWD-type wheel with some nice backspacing available.  Can't remember where on the 'Net I saw the pertaining info...<P>I haven't seen anyone do the smooth-seam thing yet,  but don't see why it won't work.  I will be diving into the body work on my GT soon,  and will seriously give this a look.  I will more than likely do it,  as the pictures I have done on the computer look REALLY good.<P>Tina,  glad I could help!  Be sure to post some pictures when it's done!<P>Brett <P><p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 03-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||jch82||03-26-2001||01:03 AM||||Oh man! That seamless look is killer!! Ever since I saw Loki's GT with the seamless look a while back I have been thinking about how you would go about doing that to a fiero. If anyone even attempts this kind of project, PLEASE be sure and post all info and as many pics of the process as possible....even if it does result in failed attempts. I still wanna see it. k? Got me!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>Those rims are about the sweetest looking one's I have ever seen....BTW, great job with the computer enhancements....what program did you use to do that?<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||4
Z||000007||fyerstarter||03-26-2001||01:13 AM||||Hehe So I'm no the only graphic artist around here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Nice work indeed. I love the seamless look and I've contemplated it many times but just seems to hard. Especially the little molding that goes below the tail-lights. Not to mention the side markers and doors are integrated into the trim. If the damn car was made of metal it would be easy, but the only option I've thought of would be doing it with fiber-glass but that's a whole lotta glass and a big hole :\<P>Well if anyone has done this or knows how please do tell. It looks like a whole new car!||||reg||1
Z||000008||TwisT||03-26-2001||01:18 AM||||I for one will be sure to keep the forum informed when this is done.  Keep an eye out...  I also have a website in the works where I'll document everything...<P>These rims are one of a handfull with the multi-peice,  "Italian" look that I want.  They look right at home on a Fiero,  just like they would on a Ferrari or such.  Alessio makes a similar wheel (called the Nevada) but it doesn't look nearly as aggressive.  It's a cheaper rim tho ($130 a peice for 18x8's!) which might justify buying them.<P>I use a few different programs for the pictures I do.  Adobe Photoshop is the best,  tho I'm not that great at it yet.  Most of the stuff I do is on a simple graphics program I got with my Lexmark printer,  called Photo Plus.  I can do about anything to a Fiero on the computer before ever touching the car.  Makes it easy to make decisions.  =)<P>Brett||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||03-26-2001||06:34 AM||||That's pretty sweet Twist.  I'm pretty good with Photoshop, never considered playing with my car until seeing how many of you guys do it.  I'll have to get some good shots of my car to try it with.<P>Anyway, I really like those wheels too.  How'd you find out the price?  I was checking out the sight, and was considering emailing the Florida rep.  They actually have a design that I like more and was interested in finding the price, so don't worry about a copy cat <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Thanks for your help <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||10
Z||000010||LZeitgeist||03-26-2001||06:58 AM||||That looks really sweet...<P>While you're playing in Photoshop, can you alter the above pic to smooth out the seams at the top of the gound effects, too, just to see what it would look like? Yu've got me curious as heck, but I don't have any of that high-end software type stuff...<P>Excellent work!!||||reg||1
Z||000011||TwisT||03-26-2001||10:13 AM||||double post<p>[This message has been edited by TwisT (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||TwisT||03-26-2001||10:18 AM||||Here's a link to one supplier:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.superbuytires.com/cgi-bin/sbtapp2?867" TARGET=_blank>http://www.superbuytires.com/cgi-bin/sbtapp2?867</A> <P>The best things to do when looking for wheels is to search the Internet first with a good search engine and to pick up a good magazine (such as Lowrider or Super Street) and type in web addresses of the different suppliers.  You can pretty much tap into every kind of wheel you can think of.<P>My original choice for wheels was actually the Antera 163,  which is VERY spendy and not all that common.  Damn good Italian looks though.<P>I'll see if maybe tonight I can tinker with the photo some more to fill the ground effects seams.  I'll be sure to post it when done.<P>||||reg||1
