Z||000051||Songman||04-10-2001||01:29 AM||||Alright Carl,<P>You asked for it... The biggest thing I did was get rid of that pine tree air freshener...     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/icons/icon10.gif">      Just teasing!<P>Really, I have always wanted to see a Fiero with wraparound taillights like on old Camaros. Thanks for giving me the chance to see it... The wraparound taillights mean that you don't need sidemarker lights any more. The taillights are also larger to make up the space where the molding had been... And I added a front quarter blinker since I got rid of the front marker light.<P>I also dropped the shadow line a couple of inches and changed the rake on it a little when I got rid of the molding and door handles.<P>And of course, I had to add the Haze Performance side air intake...<P>I left the stock top height alone. I'm 6'2" and I might want to go for a ride in this bad boy someday!<P>Oh yeah, and I also got rid of all those power lines out back there! heheh<P>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/tnfieros/smoothhaze.jpg">     <P><BR>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">     <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
